(window.LEARNC_DATA = window.LEARNC_DATA || []).push({"day": 5, "title": "Day 5", "sub": "Functions: parameters, return values, arrays as parameters", "plan": "About 20 minutes of theory, 15 minutes reading and running the 2 examples, and 60 to 90 minutes on the 4 exercises. Exercises 3 and 4 are harder: they need efficient code, not just correct code.", "goals": ["Write your own functions with parameters and a return value, and call them from <code>main</code> and from each other.", "Know that a function gets <b>copies</b> of simple values, but works on the <b>original</b> array.", "Split a longer program into small functions that each do one job (<code>isPrime</code>, <code>digitSum</code>, ...).", "Use a function inside a binary search to find the best answer of an optimisation problem."], "theory": [{"title": "Writing and calling a function", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>A <b>function</b> is a named piece of code that you write once and use many times. You have already used functions written by others (<code>scanf</code>, <code>printf</code>, <code>qsort</code>) and you have copied a few (<code>cmp</code>, <code>lower_bound</code>). The shape is: <code>return_type name(parameters) { ... return value; }</code>. The <b>parameters</b> are the inputs, <code>return</code> sends back the result and ends the function.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">digitSum</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// takes one long long, gives back an int</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">do</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">%</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">10</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">/=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">10</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">while</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// the value the caller receives</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">isEven</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// gives back 1 (true) or 0 (false)</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">%</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">2</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">==</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%lld\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">digitSum</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// call the function, keep the result</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"digit sum = %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">isEven</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">))</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"the digit sum is even</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">else</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"the digit sum is odd</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint digitSum(long long n) {          // takes one long long, gives back an int\n    int s = 0;\n    do {\n        s += n % 10;\n        n /= 10;\n    } while (n > 0);\n    return s;                        // the value the caller receives\n}\n\nint isEven(int x) {                  // gives back 1 (true) or 0 (false)\n    return x % 2 == 0;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    long long n;\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &n);\n\n    int s = digitSum(n);             // call the function, keep the result\n    printf(\"digit sum = %d\\n\", s);\n    if (isEven(s)) printf(\"the digit sum is even\\n\");\n    else printf(\"the digit sum is odd\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "12345", "out": "digit sum = 15\nthe digit sum is odd"}, {"in": "246", "out": "digit sum = 12\nthe digit sum is even"}, {"in": "0", "out": "digit sum = 0\nthe digit sum is even"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<ul>\n<li>A function must be <b>defined above</b> the place where it is used (or announced with a prototype, see Section 4).</li>\n<li><code>return</code> ends the function immediately, even in the middle of a loop. A function with return type <code>int</code> must return an int on every path.</li>\n<li>Functions that only print or change things and give nothing back have the return type <code>void</code>; they need no <code>return value;</code>.</li>\n<li>A function can call another function, for example <code>isEven(digitSum(n))</code>: the inner call runs first and its result becomes the argument of the outer one.</li>\n</ul>"}]}, {"title": "Parameters are copies", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>When you call <code>f(v)</code>, the function receives a <b>copy</b> of the value of <code>v</code>. Changing the parameter inside the function changes only the copy; the variable in the caller stays the same. To get a result out of a function, <code>return</code> it.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">void</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">addOneWrong</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// changes only the copy</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"inside: x = %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">addOne</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// send the new value back</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">v</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">5</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">addOneWrong</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">v</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"outside: v = %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">v</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// still 5</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">v</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">addOne</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">v</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// store the returned value</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"after v = addOne(v): v = %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">v</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nvoid addOneWrong(int x) {\n    x = x + 1;                       // changes only the copy\n    printf(\"inside:  x = %d\\n\", x);\n}\n\nint addOne(int x) {\n    return x + 1;                    // send the new value back\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int v = 5;\n    addOneWrong(v);\n    printf(\"outside: v = %d\\n\", v);  // still 5\n\n    v = addOne(v);                   // store the returned value\n    printf(\"after v = addOne(v): v = %d\\n\", v);\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": null, "out": "inside:  x = 6\noutside: v = 5\nafter v = addOne(v): v = 6"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Variables are private to a function.</b> The <code>s</code> in <code>digitSum</code> and a variable called <code>s</code> in <code>main</code> are two different variables. This is a good thing: every function can use short names like <code>i</code>, <code>s</code>, <code>n</code> without disturbing the others. A function can return only <b>one</b> value; if you need more, print them, or use arrays (next section).</div>"}]}, {"title": "Arrays as parameters", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>Arrays are different from single values: a function that receives an array <b>works on the original array</b>, not on a copy (copying 10<sup>5</sup> numbers on every call would be very slow). So a function can fill, reorder or change an array and the caller sees the change. Write the parameter as <code>int a[]</code>. The function does not know how many elements there are, so pass the size <code>n</code> as a separate parameter.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">void</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">readArray</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">void</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">printArray</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">sumOf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">s</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">maxPos</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// position of the first maximum</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">best</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">best</span><span class=\"p-p\">])</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">best</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">best</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">void</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">reverse</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[],</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// changes the ORIGINAL array</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-o\">--</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">tmp</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-n\">j</span><span class=\"p-p\">]</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">tmp</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">[</span><span class=\"p-mi\">100</span><span class=\"p-p\">];</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">readArray</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"sum = %lld</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">sumOf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"max is at position %d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">maxPos</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">));</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">reverse</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// a itself is now reversed</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printArray</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">a</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nvoid readArray(int a[], int n) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) scanf(\"%d\", &a[i]);\n}\n\nvoid printArray(int a[], int n) {\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n        if (i > 0) printf(\" \");\n        printf(\"%d\", a[i]);\n    }\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n}\n\nlong long sumOf(int a[], int n) {\n    long long s = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) s += a[i];\n    return s;\n}\n\nint maxPos(int a[], int n) {            // position of the first maximum\n    int best = 0;\n    for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) {\n        if (a[i] > a[best]) best = i;\n    }\n    return best;\n}\n\nvoid reverse(int a[], int n) {          // changes the ORIGINAL array\n    for (int i = 0, j = n - 1; i < j; i++, j--) {\n        int tmp = a[i];\n        a[i] = a[j];\n        a[j] = tmp;\n    }\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, a[100];\n    scanf(\"%d\", &n);\n    readArray(a, n);\n\n    printf(\"sum = %lld\\n\", sumOf(a, n));\n    printf(\"max is at position %d\\n\", maxPos(a, n));\n\n    reverse(a, n);                      // a itself is now reversed\n    printArray(a, n);\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "5\n4 -1 7 3 7", "out": "sum = 20\nmax is at position 2\n7 3 7 -1 4"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<ul>\n<li><b>Never</b> use <code>sizeof(a)</code> inside the function to get the length: there it does not mean the whole array. Always pass <code>n</code>.</li>\n<li>Use <code>const</code> in front of the type (<code>const int a[]</code>) if you want the compiler to protect an array that the function should only read. It is optional.</li>\n<li>The main program becomes short and readable: each line says <i>what</i> happens, and the details live in the functions. This is the biggest reason to use them.</li>\n</ul>"}]}, {"title": "Organising a program", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>A good function does <b>one</b> job and has a name that says which. Typical helpers: <code>isPrime</code>, <code>digitSum</code>, <code>reverse</code>, <code>check</code>. Use an <b>early return</b> when the answer is already known, and return <code>1</code> / <code>0</code> for yes / no questions. If you prefer to keep <code>main</code> first, announce the other functions at the top with a <b>prototype</b>: the same first line as the function, with a <code>;</code> instead of the body.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">isPrime</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// prototypes: \"these exist below\"</span>\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">countPrimes</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">l</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">l</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d %d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">l</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">countPrimes</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">l</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-p\">));</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">isPrime</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">2</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// early return: 0 and 1 are not prime</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">d</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">2</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">d</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">*</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">d</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">d</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">%</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">d</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">==</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// found a divisor: stop at once</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">countPrimes</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">l</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">count</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">l</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">r</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">isPrime</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">))</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">count</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">count</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint isPrime(int n);                     // prototypes: \"these exist below\"\nint countPrimes(int l, int r);\n\nint main() {\n    int l, r;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &l, &r);\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", countPrimes(l, r));\n    return 0;\n}\n\nint isPrime(int n) {\n    if (n < 2) return 0;                // early return: 0 and 1 are not prime\n    for (int d = 2; d * d <= n; d++) {\n        if (n % d == 0) return 0;       // found a divisor: stop at once\n    }\n    return 1;\n}\n\nint countPrimes(int l, int r) {\n    int count = 0;\n    for (int x = l; x <= r; x++) {\n        if (isPrime(x)) count++;\n    }\n    return count;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "1 30", "out": "10"}, {"in": "90 100", "out": "1"}, {"in": "1 1", "out": "0"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box warn\"><b>Order of the checks matters for speed.</b> When a condition combines a cheap test and an expensive one, write the cheap one first: <code>if (cheap(x) &amp;&amp; expensive(x))</code>. With <code>&amp;&amp;</code>, C stops as soon as the first part is false, so the expensive function is only called for the few numbers that pass the cheap test. This idea is the key to the third exercise.</div>"}]}], "examples": [{"title": "Narcissistic numbers", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>A number is <b>narcissistic</b> (Armstrong) if it equals the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the number of digits. For example 153 = 1<sup>3</sup> + 5<sup>3</sup> + 3<sup>3</sup>. The program prints all such numbers from 1 to N. Notice how three small functions are built on each other. Predict the output for 1000 before you run it.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">countDigits</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">do</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">/=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">10</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">while</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">c</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">power</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">base</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">e</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// base to the power e, e &gt;= 0</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">result</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">e</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">i</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">result</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">*=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">base</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">result</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">isNarcissistic</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">k</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">countDigits</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">sum</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">m</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">while</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">m</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">sum</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">power</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">m</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">%</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">10</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">k</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-n\">m</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">/=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">10</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">sum</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">==</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">n</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">N</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">N</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">first</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">for</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">N</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-o\">++</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">isNarcissistic</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">))</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-o\">!</span><span class=\"p-n\">first</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">                </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\" \"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%d\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">first</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nint countDigits(int n) {\n    int c = 0;\n    do { c++; n /= 10; } while (n > 0);\n    return c;\n}\n\nint power(int base, int e) {            // base to the power e, e >= 0\n    int result = 1;\n    for (int i = 0; i < e; i++) result *= base;\n    return result;\n}\n\nint isNarcissistic(int n) {\n    int k = countDigits(n);\n    int sum = 0, m = n;\n    while (m > 0) {\n        sum += power(m % 10, k);\n        m /= 10;\n    }\n    return sum == n;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int N;\n    scanf(\"%d\", &N);\n    int first = 1;\n    for (int x = 1; x <= N; x++) {\n        if (isNarcissistic(x)) {\n            if (!first) printf(\" \");\n            printf(\"%d\", x);\n            first = 0;\n        }\n    }\n    printf(\"\\n\");\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "1000", "out": "1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9 153 370 371 407"}, {"in": "10", "out": "1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8 9"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> <code>isNarcissistic</code> calls <code>countDigits</code> and <code>power</code>, and <code>main</code> only asks the question. The variable <code>m</code> is a working copy, because we need the original <code>n</code> at the end for the comparison <code>sum == n</code>. The result of a comparison is itself 1 or 0, so <code>return sum == n;</code> is a complete answer. The flag <code>first</code> prints a space only <i>between</i> numbers, as on Day 2.</div>"}]}, {"title": "Binary search on the answer", "parts": [{"t": "html", "html": "<p>Find the largest integer x with x &middot; x &le; N, for N up to 10<sup>12</sup>. Trying every x is too slow. But the question &ldquo;is x &middot; x &le; N?&rdquo; is <b>true for small x and false for big x</b>, with a single switching point. That is exactly the situation where binary search works: it does not search an array, it searches the <i>answer</i>. Put the test in a function <code>fits(x)</code>, and halve the range again and again.</p>"}, {"t": "code", "html": "<span class=\"p-cp\">#include</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-cpf\">&lt;stdio.h&gt;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">N</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">fits</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// is x acceptable?</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">*</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">x</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">N</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-kt\">int</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-nf\">main</span><span class=\"p-p\">()</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">scanf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%lld\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"p-n\">N</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">lo</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">hi</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1000000</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// the answer is in lo..hi (0 always fits)</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">while</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">lo</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">hi</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-kt\">long</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">mid</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">lo</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">hi</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">lo</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">+</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">)</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">/</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">2</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// round UP, see the note</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-k\">if</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">fits</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-n\">mid</span><span class=\"p-p\">))</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">lo</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">mid</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// mid works: the answer is mid or more</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-k\">else</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">            </span><span class=\"p-n\">hi</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">=</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">mid</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-o\">-</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">1</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span><span class=\"p-w\">  </span><span class=\"p-c1\">// mid is too big: the answer is smaller</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">        </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-p\">}</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-n\">printf</span><span class=\"p-p\">(</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"%lld</span><span class=\"p-se\">\\n</span><span class=\"p-s\">\"</span><span class=\"p-p\">,</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-n\">lo</span><span class=\"p-p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"p-w\">    </span><span class=\"p-k\">return</span><span class=\"p-w\"> </span><span class=\"p-mi\">0</span><span class=\"p-p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"p-p\">}</span>", "raw": "#include <stdio.h>\n\nlong long N;\n\nint fits(long long x) {                 // is x acceptable?\n    return x * x <= N;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    scanf(\"%lld\", &N);\n\n    long long lo = 0, hi = 1000000;     // the answer is in lo..hi (0 always fits)\n    while (lo < hi) {\n        long long mid = lo + (hi - lo + 1) / 2;   // round UP, see the note\n        if (fits(mid)) lo = mid;        // mid works: the answer is mid or more\n        else hi = mid - 1;              // mid is too big: the answer is smaller\n    }\n    printf(\"%lld\\n\", lo);\n    return 0;\n}", "runs": [{"in": "10", "out": "3"}, {"in": "16", "out": "4"}, {"in": "1", "out": "1"}, {"in": "1000000000000", "out": "1000000"}]}, {"t": "html", "html": "<div class=\"box note\"><b>Things to notice.</b> We look for the <i>largest</i> good value, so when <code>mid</code> works we keep it (<code>lo = mid</code>). Then <code>mid</code> must be rounded <b>up</b>, <code>(hi - lo + 1) / 2</code>: with rounding down, <code>lo = mid</code> could leave <code>lo</code> unchanged and the loop would never end (try lo = 3, hi = 4). The range shrinks from 10<sup>6</sup> to one value in about 20 rounds. Use <code>long long</code> because <code>x * x</code> reaches 10<sup>12</sup>. The same pattern, a function that answers &ldquo;does this value work?&rdquo; plus a search loop, solves the last exercise.</div>"}]}], "exercises": [{"title": "Digit toolkit", "level": "Easy", "cls": "easy", "use": "Sections 1, 2", "statement": "Given a non-negative integer n, print three things: the sum of its digits, the number written backwards (leading zeros disappear: 120 backwards is 21), and whether n is a <b>palindrome</b>, that is, whether it reads the same backwards (YES or NO).<br><br>Write the digit sum and the reversal as <b>separate functions</b> (for example <code>digitSum</code> and <code>reverseNumber</code>) and call them from <code>main</code>.", "input": ["One line with an integer n (0 &le; n &le; 10<sup>18</sup>)."], "output": ["Three values separated by spaces: the digit sum, the reversed number, and YES or NO."], "extra": "", "examples": [{"in": "12321", "out": "9 12321 YES"}, {"in": "120", "out": "3 21 NO"}, {"in": "0", "out": "0 0 YES"}, {"in": "1000000000000000000", "out": "1 1 NO"}, {"in": "7", "out": "7 7 YES"}]}, {"title": "Merge two sorted arrays", "level": "Easy - Medium", "cls": "easymed", "use": "Section 3, Day 4 (two pointers)", "statement": "You are given two arrays that are <b>already sorted</b> in increasing order. Print all their elements together, in increasing order. Do not sort again: walk through both arrays at the same time with one index for each and always take the smaller current element (two pointers, Day 4).<br><br>Write a function <code>merge</code> that takes the two input arrays, their sizes and a third array for the result, and fills it.", "input": ["Line 1: two integers n and m (1 &le; n, m &le; 10<sup>5</sup>).", "Line 2: n integers in increasing order (equal values allowed).", "Line 3: m integers in increasing order.", "All values are between -10<sup>9</sup> and 10<sup>9</sup>."], "output": ["One line with the n + m numbers in increasing order, separated by single spaces."], "extra": "Think about what happens when one of the arrays runs out before the other.", "examples": [{"in": "3 4\n1 4 9\n2 3 10 11", "out": "1 2 3 4 9 10 11"}, {"in": "1 1\n5\n5", "out": "5 5"}, {"in": "2 3\n-3 -3\n-5 -3 0", "out": "-5 -3 -3 -3 0"}, {"in": "3 1\n1 2 3\n100", "out": "1 2 3 100"}]}, {"title": "Palindromic primes", "level": "Medium", "cls": "med", "use": "Sections 1, 4, Exercise 1", "statement": "A number is a <b>palindromic prime</b> if it is a prime and also reads the same backwards (for example 131 and 11 are, but 13 and 121 are not: 13 is not a palindrome, 121 = 11 &middot; 11 is not prime). Given a range [l, r], count the palindromic primes in it and find the largest one. Use functions: <code>isPrime</code>, <code>isPalindrome</code>.<br><br><b>Time limit:</b> about 1 second for r = 10<sup>7</sup>. Testing every number with trial division up to its square root would take roughly 10<sup>10</sup> steps. Think about which of the two tests is cheap and which is expensive, and in which order to apply them.", "input": ["One line with two integers l and r (1 &le; l &le; r &le; 10<sup>7</sup>)."], "output": ["Two integers separated by a space: the number of palindromic primes in [l, r] and the largest one.", "If there is none, print <code>0 -1</code>."], "extra": "", "examples": [{"in": "1 100", "out": "5 11"}, {"in": "100 200", "out": "5 191"}, {"in": "200 300", "out": "0 -1"}, {"in": "1 10000000", "out": "781 9989899"}, {"in": "1 1", "out": "0 -1"}]}, {"title": "Cutting ropes", "level": "Hard", "cls": "hard", "use": "Sections 3, 4, Example 2 (binary search on the answer)", "statement": "You have n ropes of given integer lengths. You want to cut pieces that all have the <b>same integer length L</b> (L &ge; 1) so that you get <b>at least k pieces</b> in total. From a rope of length x you can cut <code>x / L</code> pieces (integer division); the rest is wasted. Find the <b>largest</b> L that gives at least k pieces. If even L = 1 does not give k pieces, the answer is 0.<br><br><b>Time limit:</b> about 1 second. L can be as large as 10<sup>9</sup>, so trying every L is impossible. Use a function that counts how many pieces a given L gives.", "input": ["Line 1: two integers n and k (1 &le; n &le; 10<sup>5</sup>, 1 &le; k &le; 10<sup>14</sup>).", "Line 2: n integers, the lengths of the ropes (1 &le; each &le; 10<sup>9</sup>)."], "output": ["One integer: the largest valid L, or 0 if no L works."], "extra": "Careful: the number of pieces can reach 10<sup>14</sup>, and k is read as a <code>long long</code> too. As L grows, the number of pieces never grows: that is what makes a binary search possible.", "examples": [{"in": "4 11\n802 743 457 539", "out": "200"}, {"in": "3 5\n10 20 30", "out": "10"}, {"in": "2 100\n5 5", "out": "0"}, {"in": "1 1\n1000000000", "out": "1000000000"}, {"in": "3 3\n1 1 1", "out": "1"}]}]});
